	"VersionName": "2.0.0",
	"EngineVersion": "5.8.0",
	"FriendlyName": "UEPLANE",
	"Description": "Reference-image driven scene reproduction pipeline, running inside the editor. Adds a gated workflow to Unreal's native MCP tool surface: element list -> asset list -> one-row-per-object placement table -> a three.js page the user inspects and approves -> level build (that same call freezes the approved plan and reopens it as a fresh plan + ledger + asset list for row-level edits) -> tuning (no figure, no second approval) -> surfaces -> environment -> review and iteration -> export, with a durable ledger, per-row incremental rebuilds and human-in-the-loop gates. No C++ modules; the workflow is plain Python on top of Epic's ToolsetRegistry.",
	"Category": "Editor",
	"CreatedBy": "ZHUPO233",
	"CreatedByURL": "https://github.com/ZHUPO233",
	"DocsURL": "https://github.com/ZHUPO233/UE-Planar-SceneBuilder-MCP",
